# The sacrifice is a cost (CR 118.8): paid as the spell is cast, so when Bot2 counters Corrupted Conviction the Ornithopter is still gone and Bot1 draws nothing.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Ornithopter
Corrupted Conviction
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Counterspell
Island x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Corrupted Conviction.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Counterspell.Cast(Corrupted Conviction)
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Jet
Bot1.Graveyard = Corrupted Conviction; Ornithopter
Bot2.Graveyard = Counterspell
